    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-11011",
      "problem": "If $\\cot x = 1$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $\\cot(x+5\\pi).$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y = \\cot x$ is $\\pi.$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cot{x} = \\cot{(x+n\\pi)} .\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+5\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cot{x} = 1,$ then $\\cot{(x+5\\pi)} = 1.$",
